  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CKC - Women-led development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Center for Knowledge Co-creation and Development Research (CKC) is a dynamic, non-profit organization based in Hue, Vietnam, dedicated to advancing inclusive and sustainable development. Established in 2017 under the Thua Thien Hue Union of Science and Technology Associations and certified by the provincial Department of Science and Technology, CKC conducts applied research and provides evidence-based solutions to address pressing social, environmental, and economic challenges.CKC&#x2019;s work centers on empowering marginalized and disadvantaged groups including women, people with disabilities, and ethnic minorities, through initiatives that promote social equity, environmental sustainability, and resilient livelihoods. Guided by principles of transdisciplinary collaboration and knowledge co-creation, the Center supports NGOs, government agencies, private enterprises, and communities in making informed, equitable decisions for long-term impact. Our core expertise includes project evaluation and implementation, social baseline research and impact assessment, and the development of livelihood restoration and community development plans. CKC also conducts social compliance evaluations on labor standards and ethical business practices, ensuring that projects align with both national and international frameworks. Additionally, CKC designs and implements community-based initiatives that strengthen local capacity and promote gender equality, youth leadership, and cultural preservation. Headquartered in Hue, CKC&#x2019;swork spans Central Vietnam and the wider region, including Lao PDR, reflecting our commitment to context-sensitive and inclusive development across diverse landscapes and communities. Through every activity, CKC remains steadfast in its mission to connectknowledge with action - empowering people, fostering collaboration, and creating pathways toward a more just and sustainable future.</narrative>
  </description>
